name    hackquit
prog    /dd/CMDS/GAMES/hack
# THE DOCUMENTED WAY OUT, TESTED.  DOC/START-HERE tells a new user `Q' then
# `y' to quit hack, and a person stuck in a game is the worst thing this disk
# can do to somebody.  This drives hack into the dungeon and takes that way
# out; the high-score table is what you get, and getting it means the game
# let go of the terminal.
#
# WRITTEN WITH `until', NOT WITH GUESSES.  hack takes anywhere from five to
# fifteen seconds to reach the dungeon and the first version of this script
# used fixed waits and passed about every other run.  A flaky test is worse
# than no test.
#
# EVERY MARKER BELOW IS TEXT HACK REALLY PRINTS, read out of a capture.  It
# does not ask "Who are you?" here -- it takes the name from USER -- and the
# quit confirmation is "Really quit?", not the possessions question the first
# draft guessed at.  And the dungeon drawing is not the end of the start-up:
# a `Hello tester, welcome to hack!' line arrives after it with its own
# --More--, and a Q typed before that is answered by the pager, not the game.
# There can be TWO of those: `You are lucky! Full moon tonight.' turns up on
# some runs and not others, so the script clears the pager twice.  A second
# space with nothing to clear is harmless -- hack ignores it.
rate    0.6
until   experienced player
key     n
until   Hit space to continue
key     \s
until   Level 1
until   --More--
key     \s
wait    2
key     \s
wait    2
snap    dungeon
key     Q
until   Really quit
key     y
until   quit on dungeon level
wait    2
snap    afterquit
expect  quit on dungeon level
